00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:00.950 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  a whispering batman inspired by kirk  cobain in slippers robert pattinson had  some wild ideas about how to bring  batman to life find it all right here  the batman is finally out in theaters  and there is no one better to play the  eccentric billionaire bruce wayne than  robert pattinson his version of batman  is less polished and grungier than  previous iterations and the actor has  found ways to make the role his own he  even tried to change a well-known  hallmark attributed to the franchise  batman's voice in order to disguise  himself from his alter ego bruce batman  films have always included some  alteration to the character's voice be  it christian bale's trademark gritty  roar or ben affleck's voice modulator in  the dceu films changing the voice is an  important aspect of the role not to be  outdone pattinson tried to put his own  flair on the concept though it didn't  last for very long in an attempt to  distinguish himself from his  predecessors pattinson wanted to steer  away from what audiences had come to  know as batman and do something  radically different in an interview with  jimmy kimmel live he explained how he  tried to change the voice  i just thought because everyone does  this kind of gruff gravely thing i'm  like i'm going to do the opposite as for  what pattinson decided his take was  going to be he told kimmel i'm going to  go really  whispery and i tried to do it for the  first like two weeks  and it just looked absolutely atrocious  the actor took his shot and although it  didn't immediately hit with the  production of the batman he eventually  found his stride after his first attempt  at a different voice he found a happy  medium pattinson admitted that something  seemingly happens when you put on the  suit after he found his groove he was  able to find the best voice for the film  inventions to robert pattinson's credit  what he was trying wasn't that far off  the mark with so many versions of batman  it's only natural that an actor may want  to try something new and he wasn't even  the first batman to try it when  initially trying on the costume  pattinson learned that batman veteran  christian bale had also tried to use a  similar intonation for batman begins  bale of course played an entirely  different batman where pattinson's  batman is reclusive and moody bale  emphasized bruce wayne's wealth and  privilege but even with this dichotomy  it seems that pattinson's instincts  weren't so different from bales bale has  been somewhat infamous for how dark and  rough his voice became when portraying  the batman persona though he has gotten  flack for the voice he puts on some fans  argue that it's important to  differentiate bruce wayne from batman  wayne is a recognizable figure in gotham  a local celebrity so he would need a  severe vocal change in order to protect  his identity pattinson felt comforted  that not only did bale try to do a  different voice but you can hear it in a  very early teaser trailer for the 2005  film you can also hear bale's early  voice experiment in his audition video  gotham needs you  and you serve gotham i serve justice  the voice isn't the only difference  between bale and pattinson's batman  director matt reeves has been very open  about his influences on the batman in an  interview for empire the director spoke  about how one of his main influences was  kurt cobain nirvana's something in the  way is featured heavily in the trailer  and there is a grungier aesthetic  present in the promotional materials at  first pattinson didn't agree saying  really that's kind of the opposite of  what my imagine bruce wayne to be but  eventually he started brainstorming on  the subject after his idea of the  whispering voice failed he had some  additional input pattinson joked to  jimmy kimmel that in the first costume  meeting i wanted to go like really  really really coco bane and kind of  wanted to wear like a dressing gown and  kind of fluffy like bugs bunny slippers  but the idea of grunge is still present  in this iteration of the batman even  without any whispering or flannel the  gritty aspect of the film is present in  batman's muscle car and beat up costume  and if their reactions to the batman  from fans and critics are any indication  pattinson certainly stuck the landing  despite his early vocal experiments  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you

